  <head>
    <component name='HAnim' level='1'/>
    <meta name='title' content='HAnimGimbalJointController_CastleScript.x3d'/>
    <meta name='description' content='HAnim humanoid with one large gimbal controlling one joint at a time. Logic is written in CastleScript (Castle Game Engine / castle-model-viewer). Click a joint or use PREV/NEXT, then drag the X/Y/Z rings; rotation is clamped to each joint llimit/ulimit.'/>
  </head>
  <Scene>
    <!-- Joint colours: left = blue, right = red, center = green, selected = yellow.
         Ring colours: X = red, Y = green, Z = blue.  Faded ring = axis locked (llimit == ulimit).
         NOTE: the 'limits' field of the Script repeats the llimit/ulimit values of the joints
         (CastleScript cannot read other nodes).  Keep them in sync if you edit the limits. -->
